// Auto-generated for the Unit Board — Level 3 (2001–3000字) Unit 13
window.T13_DASHBOARD_UNITS = [{"unit":1,"theme":"accurate – fist","cards":[{"w":"accurate","p":"adj.","d":"correct in all details; exact and free from error","c":"精確的；準確無誤的","s":"The scientist provided a highly accurate description of how the virus spreads among human cells.","t":"那位科學家提供了關於該病毒如何在人體細胞間傳播的極為準確無誤的描述。"},{"w":"accuracy","p":"n.","d":"the quality or state of being correct, precise, or exact","c":"準確性；精確度（不可數）","s":"The editor spent three hours checking the news article for factual accuracy before publishing it online.","t":"編輯在線上發表新聞報導之前花了三個小時檢查其事實準確性。"},{"w":"achieve","p":"v.","d":"to successfully bring about or reach a desired goal by effort","c":"實現；達成；贏得","s":"Through persistent dedication and disciplined training, the young runner managed to achieve his lifelong dream of winning Olympic gold.","t":"透過堅持不懈的奉獻與自律訓練，那位年輕跑者成功實現了他贏得奧運金牌的終生夢想。"},{"w":"achievement","p":"n.","d":"a thing done successfully, typically by effort, courage, or skill","c":"成就；豐功偉業（可數/不可數）","s":"Graduating at the top of her medical school class was a truly remarkable achievement for Angela.","t":"以醫學院第一名成績畢業對安琪拉而言確實是一項卓越的成就。"},{"w":"attract","p":"v.","d":"to cause someone to come to a place or be interested in something","c":"吸引；引起…的好感／興趣","s":"Bright flashing advertising neon signs on the avenue are designed specifically to attract the attention of passing shoppers.","t":"大道上閃爍明亮的霓虹廣告招牌專門設計用來吸引路過購物者的注意力。"},{"w":"attraction","p":"n.","d":"a feature or quality that makes something interesting or appealing","c":"吸引力；觀光勝地（可數/不可數）","s":"Living in a vibrant cosmopolitan metropolis holds great attraction for ambitious young university graduates.","t":"居住在充滿活力的大都會對雄心勃勃的年輕大學畢業生而言極具吸引力。"},{"w":"attractive","p":"adj.","d":"pleasing or appealing to the senses, mind, or eye","c":"吸引人的；有魅力的；令人動心的","s":"The multinational software company offered Jason an extraordinarily attractive salary package that he could not refuse.","t":"這家跨國軟體公司向傑森提供了一份令人難以拒絕的極為誘人且優渥的薪資福利。"},{"w":"automatic","p":"adj.","d":"operating by itself with little or no direct human control; done unconsciously","c":"自動的；不假思索的；無意識的","s":"Most modern suburban supermarkets have sliding automatic doors that open instantly as soon as customers step near.","t":"大多數現代郊區超市都配有感應滑動自動門，顧客一靠近就會立即開啟。"},{"w":"credit","p":"n.","d":"public acknowledgment or praise; an entry recording a sum received; reputation for solvency","c":"信用；功勞；學分（不可數/可數）","s":"Although the entire engineering team worked all weekend, the selfish manager took all the credit for the successful product launch.","t":"儘管整個工程團隊週末都在加班，那位自私的經理卻把產品成功發布的所有功勞攬在自己身上。"},{"w":"credit","p":"v.","d":"to publicly attribute something good to someone; to add money to an account","c":"歸功於；存入（金額）（動詞）","s":"The online store promised to credit five hundred dollars directly to my bank account within two business days.","t":"該網路商店承諾在兩個工作天內將五百元直接存入我的銀行帳戶中。"},{"w":"determine","p":"v.","d":"to firmly establish or decide after research or calculation; to control","c":"決定；查明；確定（動詞）","s":"City fire department investigators are working day and night to determine the exact cause of the downtown warehouse blaze.","t":"市消防局調查員正日夜工作以查明市中心倉庫大火的確切起因。"},{"w":"determination","p":"n.","d":"firmness of purpose; the process of establishing something","c":"決心；毅力；測定（不可數）","s":"With fierce determination and relentless courage, the injured marathon runner crossed the finish line before night fell.","t":"帶著無比堅定的決心與毅力和無畏勇氣，受傷的馬拉松跑者在夜幕降臨前跨過了終點線。"},{"w":"dip","p":"v.","d":"to put something briefly into liquid; to sink or drop temporarily","c":"浸；泡；短暫下降（動詞）","s":"On chilly winter evenings, my grandfather loves to dip crusty French bread into his hot bowl of vegetable stew.","t":"在寒冷的冬日夜晚，我祖父喜歡將酥脆的法國麵包浸入熱騰騰的蔬菜燉湯中。"},{"w":"dip","p":"n.","d":"a brief swim; a thick savory sauce for dipping food; a sudden slight drop","c":"短暫暢泳；沾醬；微跌／下跌（可數）","s":"After hiking up the steep rocky hill under the blazing sun, the tourists decided to take a refreshing dip in the cool lake.","t":"在烈日下爬完險峻的岩石山丘後，遊客們決定在涼爽的湖中暢泳一番。"},{"w":"fist","p":"n.","d":"a person's hand when the fingers are bent in toward the palm and held tightly","c":"拳頭；緊握的拳（可數）","s":"Overcome with uncontrollable anger and frustration, the boxer clenched his fist tightly and stared directly at his opponent.","t":"被無法遏止的憤怒與挫折感淹沒，拳擊手緊緊握起拳頭，直視著他的對手。"}]},{"unit":2,"theme":"glow – kidney","cards":[{"w":"glow","p":"v.","d":"to give out steady light without a flame; to look radiant with health or joy","c":"發光；容光煥發；發熱（動詞）","s":"Tiny fireflies gathered around the quiet countryside lake and began to glow brightly in the dark summer night.","t":"小螢火蟲聚集在寂靜的鄉間湖泊旁，開始在黑夜中明亮地發光。"},{"w":"glow","p":"n.","d":"a steady light produced by heat or luminescence; a warm, cheerful feeling","c":"光芒；紅潤微光；喜悅自豪感（不可數/可數）","s":"After spending two weeks relaxing at the sunny seaside resort, Jessica had a lovely healthy glow on her skin.","t":"在陽光明媚的海濱度假村放鬆了兩週後，潔西卡的皮膚散發出迷人且健康的紅潤氣色。"},{"w":"glowing","p":"adj.","d":"expressing great praise or enthusiastic approval; brightly shining","c":"極口讚譽的；熱烈稱讚的；發光的","s":"The film critic wrote a glowing review of the independent documentary, urging everyone to see it.","t":"影評人為這部獨立紀錄片寫了一篇極力稱讚的評論，力薦大家前去觀賞。"},{"w":"graduate","p":"v.","d":"to successfully complete an academic degree, course, or school","c":"畢業；取得學位（動詞，/ˈɡrædʒ.u.eɪt/）","s":"After studying civil engineering diligently for four long years, Mark will finally graduate from university next June.","t":"在勤奮學習土木工程整整四年之後，馬克終於將在明年六月從大學畢業。"},{"w":"graduate","p":"n.","d":"a person who has successfully completed a course of study or a school","c":"大學畢業生；校友（名詞，/ˈɡrædʒ.u.ət/）","s":"After working in public education for two years, David decided to apply to graduate school to pursue a master's degree.","t":"在公共教育界工作兩年後，大衛決定申請研究所以攻讀碩士學位。"},{"w":"graduation","p":"n.","d":"the receiving or conferring of an academic degree or diploma; the ceremony","c":"畢業典禮；畢業（不可數/可數）","s":"Proud parents and excited students gathered inside the grand university gymnasium for the annual graduation ceremony.","t":"引以為傲的家長與興奮的學生們聚集在宏偉的大學體育館內參加年度畢業典禮。"},{"w":"hint","p":"n.","d":"a slight or indirect suggestion, indication, or small piece of advice","c":"暗示；提示；少許（可數）","s":"The trivia riddle was so complicated that nobody in the room could guess the answer until the host gave a helpful hint.","t":"那道冷知識謎題極為複雜，直到主持人給了一個有用的提示，房間裡才有人猜出答案。"},{"w":"hint","p":"v.","d":"to suggest or indicate something indirectly without stating it openly","c":"暗示；透露（動詞）","s":"During the confidential press briefing, the cabinet minister hinted at the possibility of a nationwide tax cut next spring.","t":"在機密新聞簡報會上，內閣部長暗示了明年春季可能在全國實施減稅。"},{"w":"icy","p":"adj.","d":"covered with or consisting of ice; very cold in temperature or manner","c":"結冰的；冰冷的；冷淡刺骨的","s":"Commuting by car this morning was extremely treacherous because freezing drizzle had turned the highway into an icy sheet.","t":"今天早晨開車通勤極具危險性，因為凍雨已將整條高速公路變成了一片結冰的滑面。"},{"w":"invent","p":"v.","d":"to create or design something that has not existed before","c":"發明；創造；捏造（動詞）","s":"Alexander Graham Bell is widely recognized for his brilliant work to invent the first practical working telephone.","t":"亞歷山大·格拉漢姆·貝爾因發明第一部實用電話的傑出貢獻而廣為人知。"},{"w":"invention","p":"n.","d":"a new device, method, or process developed from study and experimentation","c":"發明；新發明之物（可數/不可數）","s":"The revolutionary invention of the internet has completely transformed global business, education, and human communication.","t":"網際網路革命性的發明徹底改變了全球商業、教育與人際溝通。"},{"w":"inventor","p":"n.","d":"a person who invented a particular process or device or who invents things as an occupation","c":"發明家；發明者（可數）","s":"A talented young inventor from Taiwan won the grand prize at the international science fair for her solar water purifier.","t":"一位來自台灣的才華洋溢年輕發明家因其太陽能淨水器在國際科學展覽會上榮獲特優大獎。"},{"w":"jealous","p":"adj.","d":"feeling or showing envy of someone or their achievements and advantages","c":"嫉妒的；吃醋的；羨慕的","s":"Rachel felt intensely jealous of her coworker when she discovered that he had been promoted to senior director.","t":"當瑞秋發現同事被升職為資深總監時，她感到無比嫉妒。"},{"w":"jealousy","p":"n.","d":"the state or feeling of being jealous; envious resentment","c":"嫉妒；吃醋（不可數/可數）","s":"Destructive feelings of professional jealousy among the research scientists ruined their teamwork and delayed the clinical trial.","t":"研究科學家之間具破壞性的職場嫉妒摧毀了他們的團隊合作，並延誤了臨床試驗。"},{"w":"keyboard","p":"n.","d":"a panel of keys that operate a computer or typewriter; a musical instrument with keys","c":"鍵盤；琴鍵樂器（可數）","s":"To work efficiently in office software programs, it is very helpful to memorize common keyboard shortcuts for copying and pasting.","t":"為了在辦公軟體程式中高效工作，記住用於複製與貼上的常用鍵盤快捷鍵非常有幫助。"},{"w":"kidney","p":"n.","d":"each of a pair of organs in the abdominal cavity of mammals, excreting urine","c":"腎臟；腰子（可數）","s":"Doctors gently explained that the elderly patient would require regular dialysis until a compatible donor organ was found for a kidney transplant.","t":"醫生親切地解釋，在找到相符的器官進行腎臟移植之前，該年長患者將需要定期洗腎。"}]},{"unit":3,"theme":"lick – republican","cards":[{"w":"lick","p":"v.","d":"to pass the tongue over a surface; to overcome or defeat","c":"舔；舐；克服解決（動詞）","s":"The excited toddler happily licked chocolate ice cream off her sticky fingers after eating dessert.","t":"那個興奮的幼童吃完甜點後高興地舔掉黏黏手指上的巧克力冰淇淋。"},{"w":"lick","p":"n.","d":"an act of passing the tongue over something; a tiny amount; a stroke","c":"舔；一小點；少許（可數）","s":"The friendly golden retriever puppy ran across the living room and gave my hand an affectionate lick.","t":"那隻友善的黃金獵犬幼犬跑過客廳，親暱地舔了我的手一下。"},{"w":"mission","p":"n.","d":"an important official assignment given to a person or group, typically involving travel","c":"任務；使命；代表團（可數）","s":"Brave firefighters embarked on a perilous rescue mission into the burning chemical factory to save trapped workers.","t":"勇敢的消防隊員展開了一場危險的搜救任務，進入燃燒的化工廠拯救受困工人。"},{"w":"missionary","p":"n.","d":"a person sent on a religious mission, especially to promote Christianity in a foreign country","c":"傳教士（可數）","s":"Father James dedicated forty years of his life working as a humble Catholic missionary in remote African mountain villages.","t":"詹姆斯神父將其畢生四十年的歲月奉獻於偏遠的非洲山村，擔任一位謙遜的天主教傳教士。"},{"w":"native","p":"adj.","d":"associated with the place or circumstances of one's birth; indigenous to an area","c":"本國的；原產的；母語的","s":"Although Cindy speaks fluent English at international conferences, her native language is traditional Mandarin Chinese.","t":"雖然辛蒂在國際會議上說著流利的英語，但她的母語是傳統的繁體中文。"},{"w":"native","p":"n.","d":"a person born in a specified place or associated with a region by birth","c":"本地人；土生土長者；原住民（可數）","s":"Robert is a proud native of London who now works as a software architect in New York City.","t":"羅伯特是一位土生土長的倫敦本地人，目前在紐約市擔任軟體架構師。"},{"w":"opportunity","p":"n.","d":"a set of circumstances that makes it possible to do something; a chance","c":"機會；良機（可數/不可數）","s":"Studying abroad on an international exchange scholarship is a golden opportunity to expand your cultural horizons and learn a new language.","t":"透過國際交換獎學金出國留學是拓展文化視野並學習新語言的千載難逢良機。"},{"w":"painter","p":"n.","d":"an artist who paints pictures; a person whose job is painting buildings","c":"畫家；油漆匠（可數）","s":"Vincent van Gogh was a misunderstood post-impressionist painter whose vibrant oil masterpieces are now celebrated worldwide.","t":"文森·梵谷是一位曾備受誤解的後印象派畫家，其色彩鮮豔的油畫傑作如今享譽全球。"},{"w":"previous","p":"adj.","d":"existing or occurring before in time or order; former","c":"先前的；以前的；上一個的","s":"Candidates with previous work experience in graphic design and digital media will be given hiring priority.","t":"具備平面設計與數位媒體先前工作經驗的應徵者將獲得優先錄用。"},{"w":"previously","p":"adv.","d":"at a previous or earlier time; before","c":"先前地；在此之前（副詞）","s":"The historic downtown theater was previously known as the Grand Opera House before being converted into a modern cinema.","t":"這家歷史悠久的市中心劇院在改建為現代電影院之前，先前曾被稱為大歌劇院。"},{"w":"rely","p":"v.","d":"to depend on with full trust or confidence","c":"依靠；依賴；信賴（動詞）","s":"Whenever Lisa encounters difficult personal dilemmas, she knows she can always rely on her mother for wise advice.","t":"每當麗莎遇到艱難的個人抉擇時，她深知自己永遠可以信賴／倚賴母親給予明智建議。"},{"w":"reliable","p":"adj.","d":"consistently good in quality or performance; able to be trusted","c":"可靠的；值得信賴的；穩妥的","s":"Journalists must verify all sensitive facts through a reliable primary source before broadcasting breaking political news.","t":"記者在播報重大突發政治新聞之前，必須透過可靠的第一手來源查證所有敏感事實。"},{"w":"republic","p":"n.","d":"a state in which supreme power is held by the people and their elected representatives","c":"共和國；共和體制（可數）","s":"The proud European nation declared itself an independent democratic republic after centuries of royal monarchical rule.","t":"在經歷了數百年的皇室君主統治之後，這個引以為傲的歐洲國家宣布自己為一個獨立的民主共和國。"},{"w":"republican","p":"adj.","d":"belonging to, characteristic of, or favoring a republic; supporting the US Republican Party","c":"共和政體的；美國共和黨的","s":"The Founding Fathers drafted the constitution to establish a strong republican form of government protected by laws.","t":"開國元勳們起草憲法，旨在建立一個受法律保障的強大共和政體。"}]},{"unit":4,"theme":"rug – structure","cards":[{"w":"rug","p":"n.","d":"a floor covering of thick woven material or animal skin; a small carpet","c":"小地毯；墊子（可數）","s":"Instead of confronting their serious financial deficit honestly, the corrupt executives tried to sweep the problem under the rug.","t":"那群貪腐的高層主管非但沒有坦誠面對嚴重的財政赤字，反而試圖將問題掩飾粉飾過去。"},{"w":"rush","p":"v.","d":"to move or act with urgent haste; to force someone to act too quickly","c":"急促行進；倉促行事；催促（動詞）","s":"After hearing that his grandfather had fallen down the stairs, Jason rushed to the city hospital without a second thought.","t":"在聽說祖父從樓梯跌落後，傑森毫不猶豫地火速趕往市立醫院。"},{"w":"rush","p":"n.","d":"a sudden quick movement toward something; a period of frantic activity","c":"匆忙；熱潮；尖峰（不可數/可數）","s":"Commuting on the downtown highway during morning rush hour is always frustrating because cars barely move.","t":"在早晨交通尖峰時刻於市中心高速公路上通勤總是令人沮喪，因為車輛幾乎動彈不得。"},{"w":"sausage","p":"n.","d":"minced meat seasoned and stuffed into a cylindrical casing","c":"香腸；臘腸（可數/不可數）","s":"At the lively night market, vendors grilled juicy Taiwanese sausage over charcoal, filling the alley with delicious aromas.","t":"在熱鬧的夜市裡，攤販在炭火上烘烤著多汁的台灣香腸，讓香氣瀰漫了整條巷弄。"},{"w":"scarf","p":"n.","d":"a piece of fabric worn around the neck or head for warmth or fashion (plural: scarves or scarfs)","c":"圍巾；披肩（可數）","s":"Grandmother lovingly spent three winter weeks knitting a soft red scarf for her newborn granddaughter.","t":"祖母慈愛地花了三個冬日星期為剛出生的孫女編織了一條柔軟的紅色圍巾。"},{"w":"slave","p":"n.","d":"a person who is the legal property of another and is forced to obey them","c":"奴隸；苦工（可數）","s":"In ancient Greek and Roman societies, thousands of captured prisoners of war were forced to labor as slave on agricultural estates.","t":"在古希臘與古羅馬社會中，成千上萬被俘虜的戰俘被迫在農業莊園中充當奴隸勞作。"},{"w":"slave","p":"v.","d":"to work excessively hard like a slave","c":"做苦工；辛勤苦幹（動詞）","s":"Instead of taking a relaxing holiday, the accounting staff had to slave through the weekend to finish auditing tax documents.","t":"會計部門人員非但沒有享受輕鬆的假期，反而必須在週末拚命苦幹以完成稅務稽核文件。"},{"w":"slavery","p":"n.","d":"the state of being a slave; the practice or system of owning slaves","c":"奴隸身分；奴隸制度（不可數）","s":"President Abraham Lincoln issued the historic Emancipation Proclamation in an enduring effort to abolish slavery across the United States.","t":"亞伯拉罕·林肯總統發表了具有歷史意義的《解放宣言》，長久致力於在全美廢除奴隸制度。"},{"w":"slippery","p":"adj.","d":"difficult to hold firmly or walk on; unreliable or elusive","c":"滑的；滑溜溜的；狡猾不可信的","s":"Hiking down the steep mountain path was hazardous because morning dew and loose mud made the rocks very slippery.","t":"走下險峻的山徑極具危險性，因為晨露與鬆軟的泥土使岩石變得非常滑溜。"},{"w":"statue","p":"n.","d":"a carved or cast figure of a person or animal, especially life-size or larger","c":"雕像；塑像（可數）","s":"Millions of international immigrants sailing into New York harbor were welcomed by the magnificent sight of the statue of Liberty.","t":"數以百萬計乘船駛入紐約港的國際移民，受到宏偉的自由女神雕像的熱烈迎接。"},{"w":"structure","p":"n.","d":"the arrangement of parts in an organic or complex whole; a building","c":"結構；構造；建築結構體（可數/不可數）","s":"City building inspectors carefully examined the high-rise tower to check for any severe structure damage following the magnitude seven earthquake.","t":"在發生規模七級地震後，市建築檢查員仔細檢查了高樓大廈，以確認是否有嚴重的結構性受損。"},{"w":"structure","p":"v.","d":"to construct, organize, or arrange according to a systematic plan","c":"精心組織；合理安排；建構（動詞）","s":"The university professor advised her students to structure their research essays logically before writing the final draft.","t":"大學教授建議她的學生在撰寫最終講稿之前，合乎邏輯地精心組織構架他們的研究論文。"}]},{"unit":5,"theme":"suburb – wipe","cards":[{"w":"suburb","p":"n.","d":"an outlying residential district of a city; the area outside a central city","c":"郊區；近郊住宅區（可數，常用複數 suburbs）","s":"Tired of noisy downtown traffic, the young married couple decided to buy a home in the peaceful suburb to raise their children.","t":"厭倦了吵鬧的市中心交通，那對年輕夫婦決定在安寧的郊區買房來撫養孩子。"},{"w":"suburban","p":"adj.","d":"relating to, situated in, or characteristic of a suburb","c":"郊區的；近郊特有的","s":"Living a quiet suburban lifestyle allows families to enjoy spacious private backyards and cleaner air away from factories.","t":"過著寧靜的郊區生活方式使家庭能夠享受寬敞的私人後院，以及遠離工廠的清新空氣。"},{"w":"suck","p":"v.","d":"to draw into the mouth by creating a vacuum; (slang) to be very bad or unpleasant","c":"吸；啜；（俚語）糟透了；差勁（動詞）","s":"I honestly admit that I suck at playing chess, but I still enjoy participating in friendly matches with friends.","t":"我坦誠承認自己下西洋棋爛透了／非常差勁，但我依然很享受與朋友進行友誼賽。"},{"w":"suck","p":"n.","d":"an act or instance of sucking liquid or food; (slang) an unpleasant condition","c":"吮吸；一口（可數）","s":"The tired toddler took a long soothing suck on his pacifier and slowly fell fast asleep in the crib.","t":"那個疲憊的幼童對著安撫奶嘴長長地吮吸了一口，接著在嬰兒床裡沉沉睡去。"},{"w":"talent","p":"n.","d":"natural aptitude, flair, or superior ability; people possessing such ability","c":"天賦；才能；人才（不可數/可數）","s":"From an early age, Mozart displayed an extraordinary natural talent for playing classical piano and composing music.","t":"莫札特從小就展現了演奏古典鋼琴與作曲的非凡自然天賦。"},{"w":"talented","p":"adj.","d":"having a natural aptitude or skill for something","c":"有才華的；才華橫溢的","s":"The school orchestra is fortunate to be led by an extraordinarily talented young violinist who won multiple international honors.","t":"學校管弦樂團非常幸運能由一位贏得多項國際榮譽、極具才華的年輕小提琴家所領導。"},{"w":"tide","p":"n.","d":"the alternate rising and falling of the sea; a powerful surge or trend","c":"潮汐；浪潮；趨勢（不可數/可數）","s":"Wise elders frequently remind young students that time and tide wait for no man, so opportunities must be seized.","t":"智慧長者經常提醒年輕學子「歲月潮汐不饒人」，因此務必及時把握良機。"},{"w":"tide sb. over","p":"v.phr.","d":"to help someone through a difficult period, especially with food or money","c":"幫助某人度過難關（特別是金錢或食物）","s":"Could you please lend me fifty dollars to tide me over until I receive my company salary on Friday?","t":"你能借我五十美元好幫我度過難關撐到星期五領取公司薪水嗎？"},{"w":"van","p":"n.","d":"a medium-sized motor vehicle used for transporting goods or passengers","c":"客貨兩用箱型車；廂型貨車（可數）","s":"A yellow postal delivery van pulled up in front of our house and dropped off three packages from abroad.","t":"一輛黃色郵政快遞廂型車停在我們家門前，送來了三個海外包裹。"},{"w":"vest","p":"n.","d":"a sleeveless garment worn on the upper body, for warmth or protection","c":"背心；防彈衣；防護背心（可數）","s":"Thanks to the high-tech Kevlar bulletproof vest he wore beneath his uniform, the police officer survived the shooting unharmed.","t":"幸虧制服下穿著高科技凱夫勒防彈背心，那位警官在槍擊事件中毫髮無損地倖免於難。"},{"w":"wipe","p":"v.","d":"to clean or dry by rubbing with a cloth or hand; to completely remove","c":"擦拭；抹去；徹底消滅（動詞）","s":"The mother gently used a soft tissue to wipe the tears from her little daughter's flushed cheeks.","t":"母親溫柔地用柔軟的面紙擦拭小女兒泛紅臉頰上的眼淚。"},{"w":"wipe","p":"n.","d":"an act of wiping; a piece of disposable cloth for cleaning","c":"擦拭；濕紙巾（可數）","s":"Always carry a small pack of antibacterial wet wipe in your backpack to clean your hands before eating outdoors.","t":"背包裡隨時備有一小包抗菌濕紙巾，以便在戶外用餐前擦拭雙手。"}]}];
